          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "Your child came in because they had a runny nose, a worsening cough, noisy breathing and was not feeding well. They were diagnosed with bronchiolitis. This is a common chest infection in young babies caused by a virus."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "We did a swab from the back of the nose. This confirmed the virus RSV, which commonly causes bronchiolitis.\n\nWhen your child arrived, their breathing was fast and their oxygen levels were low. We gave them extra oxygen to help with this. By Day 2 they no longer needed extra oxygen.\n\nBecause your child was not feeding well, we passed a small tube through the nose into the stomach to give feeds that way. By Day 2 your child was taking around 75% of feeds by mouth, so the tube was removed.\n\nWe did not give antibiotics because bronchiolitis is caused by a virus, not bacteria."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
